window.docContents[225].resolve({"/Poly/#Logical-Foundations--Poly___-Polymorphism-and-Higher-Order-Functions--Polymorphism--Polymorphic-Lists--Type-Argument-Synthesis":{"contents":"\n\nSupplying every type argument is also boring, but Lean\ncan usually infer them:\n\ndef myRepeat'' (α : Type) (x : α) (count : Nat) : List α :=\n  match count with\n  | 0        => []\n  | count' + 1 => x :: myRepeat'' _ x count'\n\n\n\n\nAlternatively, we can declare arguments implicit by\nsurrounding them with curly braces instead of parens:\n\ndef myRepeat''' {α : Type} (x : α) (count : Nat) : List α :=\n  match count with\n  | 0        => []\n  | count' + 1 => x :: myRepeat''' x count'\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Logical Foundations\u0009Poly: Polymorphism and Higher-Order Functions\u0009Polymorphism\u0009Polymorphic Lists","header":"6.1.1.2. Type Argument Synthesis","id":"/Poly/#Logical-Foundations--Poly___-Polymorphism-and-Higher-Order-Functions--Polymorphism--Polymorphic-Lists--Type-Argument-Synthesis"}});